    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee on trip TRP-00213 is placed on hold — not collected from you and not refunded to you — and the case goes to a human reviewer. Escalation is not a win for either party; it is what the policy requires when the record cannot decide the question, and it is terminal, so no money order issues.\n\nThe charge cannot be upheld under POL-NS-01. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions hold, and the driver side must carry every one. Two are met on the trip record: the driver 'arrived' event at 17:47:05 (limb (a)), and the termination at 17:53:40 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_UNREACHABLE, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises — the driver did not select DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. But limbs (b) and (c) depend on the GPS trace. EV-GPS-00213 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so nothing places the driver inside the 150 m Jurong East geofence, and limb (c) measures the 300-second TRANSPORT_HUB dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the driver's 'arrived' tap. The trip record's own 6.6-minute wait and its 395-second arrival-to-cancellation interval are the record's timeline, but the arrival marker is a status the driver set and cannot itself establish the dwell. The driver's statement that he held the bay from about 17:47 to 17:53 is his own account and does not carry the positional facts the clause requires.\n\nThe fee is not refunded either. Each refund route needs a reading the bundle does not contain. POL-NS-02 refunds only where the trace holds no qualifying in-radius fix — a missing trace is not a trace, and under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact carries no fact, so the absence cannot be read as the driver being elsewhere. POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) needs a fix to test the 17:47:05 marker against, and POL-NS-06 (short dwell) needs a measured dwell; neither can run. The rider's own exoneration route, POL-NS-04, cannot run either: EV-CHAT-00213 is MISSING (weight 0.0) even though trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 shows a log existed and is now gone, so limbs (a) and (b) are undecided and the driver's assertion that he replied to every message cannot be tested against anything. POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance test is decided from coordinates alone and there are none, and its 400 m ceiling cannot be reached on a bundle with no coordinates. Every one of these limbs is undecided rather than failed, and an undecided limb supports neither the charge nor a refund.\n\nThe escalation is mandatory on its own terms. POL-NS-09(c) requires escalation where both profiles together show two or more no-show disputes between this same rider and this same driver in the trailing 90 days. EV-RPROF-00213 and EV-DPROF-00213 both record disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2 — this is the third round between this pair — so the trigger is met, and the admissibility notes identify (c), not the POL-NS-07 anti-farming limb, as the live trigger. Independently, POL-NS-09(e) applies: the only artifact that could carry the deciding fact, the GPS trace, is impaired under POL-NS-08(b) (fewer than six fixes across the waiting window — here none at all).\n\nOther points, for completeness. The SGD 6.00 fee reconciles: it is the greater of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), which is what fee_schedule.resolution_rule prescribes, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged and the amount is not discounted. POL-NS-07 compensation to the driver (80 percent of SGD 6.00 = SGD 4.80) requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full; it is not, so no compensation is payable and no driver payment is funded out of this fee. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 3 against a threshold of 4, and 3/107 = 2.8 percent against 8 percent), so it neither withholds compensation nor adds an instruction to the escalation packet. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 2, below the threshold of 3, and prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter that may not be substituted for it (POL-GEN-01).\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: obtain or reconstruct EV-GPS-00213 and EV-CHAT-00213, or the device-level data behind them, so it can be settled whether the driver was inside the Jurong East geofence for a continuous 300 seconds, and whether the rider's three messages went unanswered for 120 seconds. Those are the two tests the missing artifacts were meant to decide."
